        <body>
            <div xml:id="d241">

                <pb facs="0474" n="460" xml:id="pg460"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.01/9–844</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 4535</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-14">September 14,
                        1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretary of State encloses herewith a copy of a memorandum received from the
                    Combined Chiefs of Staff together with its enclosure entitled “Directive from
                    the Combined Chiefs of Staff to Supreme Allied Commander, Mediterranean.” The
                    directive concerns the planning for military government in Austria and, in
                    compliance with the request of the Combined Chiefs of Staff, the Ambassador is
                    instructed to present it to the European Advisory Commission for
                    information.</p>



